  "source": "tune, words and harmony from Cecil J. Sharp, English Folk-Chanteys (Simpkin, Marshall, Hamilton, Kent & Co. and Schott & Co., London; Barnicott & Pearce, Taunton, 1914), No. XXVII, \"Haul Away, Joe\", p. 32 (note p. 70: sung by John Short at Watchet), in C dorian and written here a semitone up in C# dorian; verses 1, 2 and 4 of Sharp's eleven (verse 3 left out); read from the scan at archive.org/details/englishfolkchant00shar"
